  message: "Dogfood tranche 05 facet (F85.A2 / anon-card-001): the entrypoint sub-floor breach is dominated by AND exhaustive within the library_export kind — ALL 46 library_export entrypoints sit below the 0.70 floor (min 0.185, max 0.675), no member ever reaches 0.70, accounting for 46 of the 81 sub-floor entrypoints. The floor is structurally unreachable for that kind, not a long tail. Other kinds below floor: shell_script 29, main_function 6. Evidence: frozen substrate.json entrypoints[] confidence-by-kind histogram. Blind severity 4/5, reproduced on frozen substrate."  # 4205
- op: discuss  # feb8
  at: '2026-06-06T10:37:02Z'  # feb8
  by: agent  # feb8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # feb8
  clock: 4  # feb8
  nonce: feb8  # feb8
  message: "Related distinct facet: the discrete 4-tier MODEL is fictional at the output layer (blind-severity-derived priority signal: P1). Beyond the range breaches this item tracks (below-0.70 floor, 0.95 ceiling), the published entrypoints[].confidence is a CONTINUOUS post-adjustment composite: 51 distinct values over 104 entrypoints (min ~0.185, max 1.0), only 2/104 landing on any documented tier value {0.70,0.85,0.95,0.99}. Detection emits clean tier values (0.99/0.95/0.85/0.70) then a post-detection pipeline mutates every value via additive connectivity boosts and multiplicative test/vendor/utility penalties. So §1144's 4-tier discrete table is unreachable at the output layer, and 13/104 entrypoints sit ABOVE the documented 0.99 ceiling (all at 1.0, dominated by http_route 8/13). Fix: reconcile the §1144 tier table with the §895 adjustment description — document published confidence as a continuous composite. (The undocumented additive in-degree boost was split out as its own work item — separate doc/remove fix.)"  # feb8
